// Toybox Twister — the toy store's big hall (GDD §7.1, art bible §3.2). ~1170 u, 3 laps, indoor ★★★.
// Format and conventions: docs/design/rc_track.md; environment notes: docs/design/env-toy.md.
//   cargo run -p rc_track --example plot -- toybox_twister [--rev] [--mirror]
// The orange ToyTrack ribbon (top at y = 0.3) on the teal play-mat (y = 0.05) of a 220 × 190 u
// hall (20 u ceiling, rounded corners) divided into rooms; the track crosses each wall through a
// light-up archway. Forward = clockwise. Lap: start
// straight (west) with a hop through a light-up arch → raised banked T1 → two rainbow tunnels →
// raised esses → a 2¼-turn double helix around the play castle climbing to 11.1 u → the bridge
// along the north wall and its drop jump → descent into the raised NE turn → the east straight
// through the archway gate, a hop and a third tunnel → flat hairpin → infield straight (the Rev
// jump) → banked U-turn with the shortcut and the Golden Battery table → the dollhouse → S-bend →
// fourth tunnel → raised final hairpin. Pillars under raised stretches are generated:
//   python3 tools/blender/props/toy/supports.py assets/maps/toybox_twister/track.ron --keep-out -64,-62,10.3
// Out-of-reach decor (bunting, fairy lights, balloons, signs) is in decor.ron.
(
    style: ToyTrack,
    start: 0,
    kill_height: -5,
    wall_height: 1.2,
